#91500
"Tavern on the Green"
"A tall, narrow wooden counter runs the entire length of this room, interrupted

only by swinging doors of the same height near the left end.  The wood is damp

to the touch and has started to rot slightly, filling the air with an earthy

smell.  Pictures yellow with age hang randomly about the walls, depicting

local citizens long lost to the ages.  Behind the counter are several shelves

packed tight with bottles of various shapes and heights, each filled with

liquids identified on their labels.  A narrow door leads into the back

storeroom, presumably stocked with more alcohol and food.  The counter

continues to the north, extending all the way to the building's outer wall.

"
