#91502
"Tavern on the Green Store Room"
"Floor to ceiling shelves have been built into all four walls, making the room

feel small and cramped.  The shelves are stuffed full with bottles and small

packages of snack food.  The bottles are quite dusty, implying they have been

sitting here for quite some time.  A small pool of amber-colored liquid is

dripping from a small fissure on the side of a barrel in the southwest corner

of the room.  A sour stench wafts up from the barrel, its contents spoiled

from exposure to the air.  The floor here is made of worn wooden planks,

tightly nailed together except for a few loose planks near the barrel.

