"barrel"
"This barrel is made from extremely dark colored wood with a red tinge to it.

Its texture is coarse and several splinters are protruding from the surface.

A tiny crack in the side is allowing the contents to leak out, forming a small

puddle at the barrel's base.  As the crack is allowing air to get into the

container, its contents has clearly spoiled, and emits a strong odor into the

air.

"
E
"planks"
"Wood cut from nearby trees was used to make this planking when the tavern was

built several decades ago.  From age and heavy use, the wood has been worn

down and smoothed.  Its is difficult to gain sure footing in here, from the

layers of dirt, dust, and other various substances.  In the southwest corner

of the room, a few planks are warped and raised slightly from the rest of the

floor, as the nails that should hold them down are missing.

"
