#91505
"Dome Shaped Passage"
"The ladder ends here, in a great dome-shaped passage.  The floor is outlined

in ash-colored stone, but the walkway itself is the same soft dirt as the

walls.  The walkways continue in all directions, each leading to a different

area of the underground lair.  The room is quiet and still, as not many care

to venture this deep into the earth.  A stone wall has been constructed around

the enormous pit in the center of the room.  A peek over its edge reveals

dark, murky water - too dark to observe any life that may thrive in it.  On

the wall opposite the ladder, a great tapestry hangs.  Obviously a work of a

master weaver, crimson thread spells out \"CoRD\" across the coal background,

with three ashen serpents entwined around the letters.

