tapestries hang from the vaulted ceilings and land in a soft pile near the

floor on both the east and west walls.  The floor is covered in a velvety,

dark green moss, obviously the work of some magic.  The north wall is nearly

covered by a richly illustrated map of the lands.  A great oak table fills the

center of the room, with the tattered remains of scrolls, spell books and

other sorcerer's paraphernalia piled atop it.  Aside from the poorly managed

desk, the room is void of any other extraneous objects, except for a large

dragonhide chair resting quietly behind the desk.

