"Gnoggh's Room"
"This ample chamber, lit by a series of stone braziers in the northern and

southern walls, contains a series of wooden display cases, shelves, a sturdy

looking mohogany bed, and a wide well cushioned couch.  Beside the bed, which

is in the northeast corner, sits a large grey-flecked marble desk with dark

wooden inlay.  Hanging on the northern most wall behind the bed and desk is a

faded tapestry, the subject of which seems to be some unholy ritual involving

elves, knives, butter, and some very excited ogres.  The only visible exit is

a heavy wooden door in the western wall.

